    <string name="russian_services_hint">"Banking, Gosuslugi, Yandex, VK and shopping services connect directly, as if VPN were off. They see your regular IP address, not the node’s. Apps can still ask Android whether VPN is on."</string>
    <string name="bypass_apps_hint">"Selected apps connect to the internet directly. Useful if an app does not work over VPN."</string>
    <string name="mode_nodes_hint">"Фарватер remembers a node for allowlists and one for regular blocks. When the network mode changes, it switches to the node you chose for that mode. The mode is detected automatically when Auto is selected in Sources."</string>
    <string name="failover_hint">"If the connected node stops responding, Фарватер tests backup nodes from the last check and switches to a working one, first from the same subscription, then from others. At most once every two minutes."</string>
    <string name="autostart_hint">"To enable always-on VPN, open the settings next to Фарватер and turn on Always-on VPN. Some manufacturers use a different name. You can also block internet access without VPN there.\n\nAuto-connect also works after updating Фарватер if VPN was on. Xiaomi, Huawei, Honor, OPPO and vivo also require autostart permission, described under Background activity."</string>
    <string name="security_hint">"The server owner can see which sites you visit. HTTPS protects the content. Do not enter passwords on sites without a padlock or through public nodes. Фарватер’s internal proxy is always password-protected so other apps cannot use the tunnel."</string>
    <string name="hwid_hint">"Subscriptions with device limits may need HWID to return the full list. It is a random ID for this installation, unrelated to your phone. Only your own subscriptions receive it. Tap HWID to copy."</string>
    <string name="dead_group_hint">"Nodes that fail twice in a row go into a collapsed Not responding group and are not selected automatically. The connected node is tested through its tunnel. While VPN is on, failures of other nodes in the same subscription are not counted: paid subscriptions often block a second connection. Turn off to keep these nodes in their subscriptions."</string>
    <string name="duplicates_hint">"Фарватер always removes identical links with different names. This option also hides nodes with the same address, port and protocol, even if their SNI, Reality key, TLS fingerprint, user or transport differ. It keeps the selected node in each group, or the first one in the subscription. The others are hidden, not tested and not used when looking for a working node. Off by default: another node in the group may work when the remaining one does not."</string>
